      "failure": null,
      "answer": {
        "label": "confirmed",
        "reason": "The roadmap explicitly says the durable relative consumer remains open and the pure policy and initial service are not wired into maintenance. The pinned implementation contradicts that wiring claim: persistent standalone and Ingress compositions bind a recurrence worker to application lifetime. Its polling tick constructs RelativeMaintenance, source ingestion and RelativeLifecycle together. The dispatcher calls initial materialization and then consumes persisted lifecycle sources. Initial materialization saves an occurrence, slot and continuation; lifecycle consumption checks scope, original evidence and prior outcomes, generates successors and records completion. It also invokes successor_disposition and applies protected cancellation/reconciliation. Installation and household checks, shutdown checks and replay handling constrain these effects rather than disabling the route. This establishes implemented maintenance integration, not completion of every broader recurrence acceptance obligation. No comparison base was supplied, so this verdict concerns the pinned documentation mismatch, not when it arose.",
