      "answer": {
        "label": "refuted",
        "reason": "The native input does not fill the painted control horizontally. The control has 16px left/right padding and no border; its flex input occupies the content area, so width:100% does not extend it into that padding. Thus (4,4) is in the control’s left padding, not the input. The label ignores pointer events and the underline pseudo-element does too. The test mounts the field without a padding override and is included in the Chromium browser project. Clicking that padding targets the control; its click handler explicitly focuses the input, explaining how the target assertion and enabled/readonly focus assertion can both hold. Disabled native inputs cannot be focused by that handler. The proposed input-hit explanation is contradicted by the implementation.",
